# C coursework project

This is Razvan Arhip`s submission for the C coursework.

## Usage

The program generates a map based on templates, or at random, which contains multiple markers and obstacles, and a 'robot' that 
solves the maze. 

I have included instructions for compiling and running under, for changing the map there is a input.txt in the input directory;
it admits the following keywords: 'EMPTY' 'RANDOM' 'CUSTOM' 'STAGE1' 'STAGE2' 'STAGE3' 'STAGE4' 'STAGE5'. 
The keywords must be in all caps and the only thing in the input file, the program comes with stage 5 already there.
The stages, empty, and random keywords don`t require aditional input but the custom one allows the creation of personal map
which requires aditional input, see the custom.txt file for more information on how it should be done 

## Commands for compiling

I have included a makefile for ease of use, just using the make command and then running the program should suffice,
the makefile also allows make clean for reamoving the .o files:
```
make
make clean
```
In case that does not work either of these 2 commands should work, if used from the main directory:
```
gcc $(find input drawing_logic robot_logic -type f -name '*.c') -o main -lm
```
```
gcc input/stages.c input/read.c drawing_logic/drawings.c drawing_logic/graphics.c robot_logic/robot_navigation.c robot_logic/robot.c -o main -lm
```

## Command for running

'''
./main | java -jar drawapp-4.5.jar
'''

## On Randomness

I have decided to use a set seed for the rand() function, which is 235; this cand be disabled by deleting 
the first line of code in the main function and replacing it with the one commented below it.

